{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"47570d56-8bcd-47b4-b033-ec1a680ddc7b","status":"SUCCESS","response":"### Target Files\n- `models.py`\n- `matcher.py`\n- `audit.py`\n- `policy_engine.py`\n\n### Symbols \u0026 Line Ranges\n- `models.py`:\n  - `Role.__post_init__` (lines 10-11)\n- `matcher.py`:\n  - `valid_resource` (lines 2-3)\n  - `matches` (lines 6-7)\n- `audit.py`:\n  - `AuditLog.record` (lines 9-16)\n- `policy_engine.py`:\n  - `PolicyEngine.resolve_roles` (lines 17-26)\n  - `PolicyEngine.decide` (lines 28-43)\n\n### Invariants \u0026 Exact Changes\n- **`models.py` — `Role.__post_init__`**:\n  - Currently assigns `self.parents` as-is. Change to `object.__setattr__(self, \"parents\", tuple(self.parents))` so `parents` is always copied to an independent tuple.\n  - `Rule` and `Decision` already satisfy the frozen dataclass and `effect in (\"allow\", \"deny\")` (`ValueError`) requirements.\n- **`matcher.py` — `valid_resource(resource)`**:\n  - Must return `False` if `not isinstance(resource, str)` or `not resource`.\n  - Reject leading/trailing `/` (`resource.startswith(\"/\") or resource.endswith(\"/\")`), empty segments (`\"\"` in `resource.split(\"/\")`), standalone `\".\"` or `\"..\"` segments, backslashes, `%`, `?`, `#`, `*`, or any non-ASCII-alphanumeric/underscore/dot/hyphen character.\n  - Concretely: split by `\"/\"` and verify each segment is non-empty, not in `(\".\", \"..\")`, and matches `^[A-Za-z0-9._-]+$` (ASCII only, e.g. `re.fullmatch(r\"[A-Za-z0-9._-]+\", seg)`). Do not normalize paths.\n- **`matcher.py` — `matches(pattern, resource)`**:\n  - Reject immediately if `not valid_resource(resource)` or `not isinstance(pattern, str)` or `not pattern`.\n  - If `pattern == \"*\"`, return `True`.\n  - If `pattern.endswith(\"/*\")`: let `prefix = pattern[:-2]`; return `valid_resource(prefix) and resource.startswith(prefix + \"/\")` (matches descendants at a slash boundary, not `prefix` itself, and rejects malformed prefixes).\n  - Otherwise: return `valid_resource(pattern) and pattern == resource` (exact match for valid literal paths; all other wildcard forms or malformed patterns fail closed with `False`).\n- **`audit.py` — `AuditLog.record(subject, roles, action, resource, decision)`**:\n  - Remove the `if not decision.allowed: return` early return so that every decision (including invalid resources, explicit denies, and implicit denies) appends an entry.\n  - Keep `deepcopy({...})` with `\"subject\": subject, \"roles\": list(roles), \"action\": action, \"resource\": resource, \"allowed\": decision.allowed, \"reason\": decision.reason`.\n- **`policy_engine.py` — `PolicyEngine.resolve_roles(roles)`**:\n  - Currently loops infinitely on cycles because `resolved` is not checked before re-queuing parents.\n  - Add `if name in resolved or name not in self.roles: continue` before `resolved.add(name)` and `pending.extend(self.roles[name].parents)` so cycles terminate without losing any reachable roles.\n- **`policy_engine.py` — `PolicyEngine.decide(subject, roles, action, resource)`**:\n  - Currently returns `matching[0].effect` (wrong reason `\"deny\"` instead of `\"explicit_deny\"`, and wrong precedence if an `\"allow\"` rule appears before a `\"deny\"` rule).\n  - Evaluate all matching rules:\n    - If any matching rule has `rule.effect == \"deny\"`, set `decision = Decision(False, \"explicit_deny\")`.\n    - Else if any matching rule has `rule.effect == \"allow\"`, set `decision = Decision(True, \"allow\")`.\n    - Else set `decision = Decision(False, \"no_matching_allow\")`.\n  - Keep `invalid_resource` check returning `Decision(False, \"invalid_resource\")` and `self.audit.record(subject, roles, action, resource, decision)` for all paths.\n\n### Verify Command\n- `pytest -q --tb=short`\n","duration_seconds":9.529925500000001,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":28366,"output_tokens":1523,"thinking_tokens":110,"cache_read_tokens":22247,"total_tokens":29889}}}
